renderer: smooth upscaled DRCS, and map a few more DRCS patterns

DRCSRenderer scaled DRCS bitmaps with nearest neighbour. At common
output sizes a 36x36 pattern (often an 18x18 glyph sent pixel-doubled)
ends up 4x enlarged, so unmapped kanji and symbols look very jagged
next to font-rendered text.

Drop duplicated rows/columns (lossless), enlarge with Scale2x to round
off staircase diagonals, then finish with bilinear sampling so edges are
anti-aliased. Adds test/drcs_smooth with synthetic patterns.

Also map patterns seen on Japanese terrestrial broadcasts (2026-10):
one-dot shinnyou 迂 (U+8FC2), 《 》 and half-width ｟ ｠.

